---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import MusicPlayer from '../components/MusicPlayer.astro';
import { screenPicks } from '../data/culture';
---
<Base title="Interests" description="Music, anime, Formula 1, technology, markets and other interests that shape how Aryan Basantani sees the world.">
  <header class="page-head interests-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Away from the work log</p>
    <h1>The things I keep returning to.</h1>
    <p>Soundtracks, strange futures, fast cars, chips, markets, and questions with more than one good answer.</p>
  </header>

  <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Interest sections">
    <a href="#music">Music</a><a href="#screen">Anime & film</a><a href="#formula-one">Formula 1</a><a href="#technology">Technology</a><a href="#markets">Markets & geopolitics</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="music" class="interest-chapter" aria-labelledby="music-title">
    <div class="chapter-intro"><p class="mono">01</p><h2 id="music-title">Music</h2><p>Joe Hisaishi for wonder. Hans Zimmer for scale. Anime openings when subtlety can wait.</p></div>
    <MusicPlayer />
  </section>

  <section id="screen" class="interest-chapter" aria-labelledby="screen-title">
    <div class="chapter-intro"><p class="mono">02</p><h2 id="screen-title">Anime, films and series</h2><p>Dragon Ball Z is still the favourite. The wider list leans psychological, speculative and quietly adventurous.</p></div>
    <div class="anilist-shelf" data-anilist-root data-anilist-user="arbs42">
      <div class="anilist-meta-bar">
        <div class="anilist-meta-lead">
          <span class="anilist-status-wrap">
            <i class="anilist-dot" data-anilist-dot aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span data-anilist-status>Personal AniList ratings · @arbs42</span>
          </span>
          <span class="anilist-stats mono" data-anilist-stats hidden></span>
        </div>
        <div class="anilist-meta-actions">
          <a class="anilist-profile-link mono" href="https://anilist.co/user/arbs42/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-anilist-profile>
            <span>anilist.co/user/arbs42</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <button type="button" class="anilist-refresh" data-anilist-refresh hidden>Refresh</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="anilist-group" data-anilist-watching hidden>
        <div class="anilist-subhead">
          <div>
            <p class="mono">CURRENTLY WATCHING</p>
            <h3>On screen right now</h3>
          </div>
          <span class="anilist-count mono" data-anilist-watching-count></span>
        </div>
        <div class="screen-strip anilist-watching-strip" data-anilist-watching-strip></div>
      </div>

      <div class="anilist-group" data-anilist-favorites hidden>
        <div class="anilist-subhead">
          <div>
            <p class="mono">ALL-TIME FAVORITES</p>
            <h3>The ones that stayed</h3>
          </div>
          <span class="anilist-count mono" data-anilist-favorites-count></span>
        </div>
        <div class="screen-strip anilist-favorites-strip" data-anilist-favorites-strip></div>
      </div>

      <div class="anilist-group" data-anilist-top>
        <div class="anilist-subhead anilist-subhead-filterable">
          <div>
            <p class="mono">TOP RATED</p>
            <h3>Highest personal scores <span class="anilist-count mono" data-anilist-top-count>{screenPicks.length}</span></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="screen-filters" hidden>
            <button type="button" data-screen-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
            <button type="button" data-screen-filter="Film" aria-pressed="false">Films</button>
            <button type="button" data-screen-filter="Series" aria-pressed="false">Series</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="screen-strip" data-anilist-top-strip>
          {screenPicks.map(item => (
            <a href={item.url} class="screen-card" data-format={item.format} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <div class="screen-cover">
                <img src={item.cover} alt="" width="150" height="220" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer"/>
                <span>{item.score}<small>/10</small></span>
              </div>
              <small>{item.format}</small>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="interest-duo" aria-label="Formula 1 and technology">
    <article id="formula-one" class="interest-chapter">
      <div class="chapter-intro"><p class="mono">03</p><h2>Formula 1</h2></div>
      <p>Max Verstappen and Red Bull pulled me in. I stay for the engineering: how regulation, upgrade opportunities, packaging and driver decisions change what happens on track.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="technology" class="interest-chapter">
      <div class="chapter-intro"><p class="mono">04</p><h2>Technology</h2></div>
      <p>I like trying out Linux distros, reading about fintech products and market systems, and experimenting with the rapidly changing world of AI agents. Lately that means spending time with tools like Codex, OpenCode, Antigravity, and different CLI/harness setups to see what actually improves how I build and work.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section id="markets" class="interest-chapter interest-wide" aria-labelledby="markets-title">
    <div class="chapter-intro"><p class="mono">05</p><h2 id="markets-title">Finance, markets and geopolitics</h2></div>
    <p>I follow the path from a large shift to an everyday consequence: oil prices, geopolitics, chip shortages, DRAM and SSD supply, and why the long trend toward cheaper technology sometimes breaks.</p>
    <a class="section-action" href="/work/semiconductor-research/"><span>See the semiconductor research</span><svg class="btn-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 11.5 11.5 4.5M6 4.5h5.5V10"/></svg></a>
  </section>
</Base>
